## Phase A-2: Realistic monopile on soil springs

Extends the validated beam model to a realistic offshore wind foundation: pile in the
seabed, transition piece, tapered tower and nacelle/rotor. Soil is modelled with
distributed springs (k = n_h x depth) and the submerged part carries hydrodynamic added mass.
The first natural frequency and mode shapes are computed for four installation stages.

| Stage | f1 (Hz), medium soil |
|---|---|
| Bare monopile | 1.22 |
| + Transition piece | 0.86 |
| + Tower | 0.51 |
| + Nacelle and rotor | 0.26 |

**Key findings**
- Every installed part lowers the natural frequency.
- Soft soil and the water around the pile lower it further, mostly for the bare pile.
- The tower standing without the rotor is the stage to check for wind-induced vibration (VIV) in Phase B.

All values are illustrative, not site data.

